    "measurementTechnique": [
      "Pre-dawn and midday shoot water potentials of each tree were measured monthly using Scholander-type pressure chambers (PMS Instruments, Albany, OR, USA). Two healthy twigs were collected from south-facing branches before sunrise and between 1130 and 1300 h, placed in a humidified plastic bag and stored in a cooler until water potential was measured within 2 h ofcollection.",
      "P012 excluded due to small size"
